/-!
# Source-specific Griess (1990) tau-real rational product table

Original source: Robert L. Griess Jr., J. Algebra 131 (1990), 281–293,
DOI 10.1016/0021-8693(90)90176-O.
Source generation formula: e_x ∘ e_y = (-2)^(-c(x,y)) ω^g(x,y)e_(x+y),
g = -x₁x₂y₃ - x₃y₁y₂ + x₂x₃y₁ + x₁y₂y₃ mod 3.
x,y are lexicographic F₃³ labels; c=1 when linearly independent, else 0.
Tau-fixed basis: e0; (e_a+e_-a, ωe_a+ω²e_-a) for the 13 lexically
first antipodal representatives. Coefficients obtained using exact BigInt
Q(ω)=Q[t]/(t²+t+1) arithmetic, NOT floating point.

This source table and native target use the EXISTING native
Integration.RationalAlbertNative.RationalAlbert.jordanProduct and the
27×27 witness from Integration.Griess1990RationalTrialityMatrixWitness.

A finite reflected product acceptance theorem is SOURCE-WRITTEN below.
No Lean/Lake kernel receipt in this environment. A successful 729
check establishes a finite product basis correspondence only once the
source table is also formally tied to Griess's formula; it does not
magically identify Monster weight-two, physics, KK, RH or E6.
-/

